{%- comment -%}
  Renders an article's position in its blog's sequence as a zero-padded three
  digit string ("001", "012").

  The number comes from the custom.story_number metafield rather than from the
  loop, so every place that shows it agrees: each blog runs its own sequence,
  and only published posts hold a number. Deriving it from forloop position
  instead would drift the moment a post in the middle is unpublished — the grid
  would renumber what follows it while the article's own hero caption kept the
  old value.

  `fallback` covers a post with no number yet: an unpublished one being
  previewed in the theme editor, or one published since the last renumber.
  Pass the loop position so such a post still shows something sensible.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'story-number', article: article, fallback: forloop.index -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign n = article.metafields.custom.story_number.value | default: fallback | default: 0
  assign padded = '00' | append: n | slice: -3, 3
  echo padded
-%}
